    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Related\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41634\n\n### Problem\n\nHow to know whether following mode is enabled to toggle it programmatically?\n\nTake `vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor`, for example. Should it move only the main cursor or all cursors at once (see https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41634)? Both behaviors are useful, but temporarily toggling following mode is easier than trying to follow all cursors programmatically.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMaybe:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_get_mode().mcursor_following\n```",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "An API is planned, but in general it shouldn't be necessary for plugins to care. If `nvim_win_set_cursor` is called by a mapping, when it cascades per-cursor the mapping acts as if the current cursor is the main cursor, and thus should just work (or there's a bug in multicursor). \n\nSo the details matter, i.e. need a concrete use-case in this report.",
