        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "A usecase I came across is the need to restore following mode state before/after a keymap.\nE.g. I have 2 keymaps currently, that always end with following mode disabled:\n`vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Up>\", \"Qk\")` and `vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Down>\", \"Qj\")`\n\nIdeally I'd like these keymaps to keep the following mode state before/after, but, if I understood correctly, that would currently require me to manually create the mark with `vim.api.nvim_mcursor` manually and then move the cursor in way that won't cascade regardless of following mode(Or maybe the creation prevents cascade anyway?).\n\nIn general I think keymaps that create new multicursors could benefit from knowing when following mode is active.",
